Organization = {China Univ Petr; Taiwanese Inst Knowledge Innovat},
Abstract = {Fires cause massive harm and damage to families, even though people know
   to prevent fire, they do not have the correct concepts, and they
   overlook the safety of children. Thus this study considers that children
   recognize few words, and creates graphics as research samples to survey
   the perceptions of 5-7 year old children regarding unsafe act causing
   fires, in order to understand their perceptions of acts that cause fires
   in home life. Graphical questionnaire survey and interview method were
   applied in this study, 24 children participated in this survey. The
   results indicate that (1) half of the children have preliminary
   understanding of unsafe; (2) the error rate of removing power cords is
   the highest, and should be related to the fact that children have
   already formed the habit of removing power cords; (3) Setting off
   firecrackers had the highest error rate, and is the unsafe act that
   children need to pay most attention to; (4) good understanding for using
   a lighter to set curtains on fire, and also know to put lighters on
   cabinets so they cannot take them; (5) good understanding of using the
   gas stove being an unsafe act that will lead to fires; (6) boys and
   girls have a significant difference in pulling out plugs with wet hands,
   pulling out power cords, setting off firecrackers, mother using the
   fire, and using fire without anyone around, and girls have better
   knowledge of unsafe acts causing fire than do boys.},
