   Regulatory Purposes, OOSTENDE, BELGIUM, MAY 06-09, 1996},
Organization = {Initiat Harmonizat Atmospher Dispers Modelling Regulatory Purposes},
Abstract = {A summary presentation is made of representative samples from a
   comprehensive experimental databank on car exhaust dispersion in urban
   street canyons. Physical modelling, under neutral stratification
   conditions, was used to provide visualization, pollutant concentration
   and velocimetry measurements above and inside test canyons amidst
   surrounding urban roughness. The study extended to two different canyon
   aspect ratios, in combination with different roof configurations on the
   surrounding buildings. To serve as a reliable basis for validation and
   testing of urban pollution dispersion codes, special emphasis was placed
   on data quality assurance.},
