Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers Geoscience
   \& Remote Sensing Soc},
Abstract = {This work is framed within Urban GEO BIG DATA, a project of national
   interest funded by the Italian Ministry of Education, University and
   Research aimed to set up methodologies to investigate and manage urban
   areas benefiting of available Geo Big Data and Free and Open Source
   Software (FOSS). Five Italian cities (Turin, Milan, Padua, Rome, and
   Naples) are examined with respect to: 1) urban mobility; 2) land cover
   and soil consumption at different resolutions; 3) displacement time
   series. Here we focus on the main outcome of the project, that is the
   implementation of a collaborative Free and Open Source (FOS) distributed
   and acentric interoperable geospatial data infrastructure consisting of
   several components, with respect to land cover and soil consumption.
   Main features and possible user applications of this platform are
