   on Life in the Mediterranean Region, Thessaloniki, GREECE, OCT 08-12,
   2005},
Organization = {Mediterranean Sci Assoc Environm Prot},
Abstract = {This paper presents a short-term forecasting prototype, O-3-AFM
   (Ozone-Adaptive Fuzzy Model), of hourly urban ozone (O-3) concentrations
   at two spatial points of interest, when presented with inputs Of O-3
   source emissions measured at one of the above points. The structure of
   the O-3-AFM, which combines characteristics from the Neural Networks and
   the Fuzzy Logic methodologies, allows for its adaptability and function
   upon real-time data. By means of the AFM 2.0 (Adaptive Fuzzy Modeller,
   of STMicroelectronics, 1998) software and real data from pollution
   monitoring stations in the city of Athens, Greece, two O-3-AFM scenarios
   were developed, which performed over varying forecasting time periods.
   Considering the fact that, the O-3-AFM functions only upon an indirect
   indicator of stagnating conditions (CO concentration), its performance
   was validated by means of specific performance indexes and found to be
   quite satisfactory and promising, yet leaving space for further
   refinement e.g., upon larger data records. The proposed approach can
   highly contribute to the support of a reliable, on time decision-making
   process for the initiation of tactics towards the control of the urban
   pollution episode.},
