Abstract = {The rapid development of urban areas is not only a contributor to the
   economic growth of developing countries but also a significant driver of
   environmental change and resource use. Achieving sustainable development
   of urban areas requires an understanding of the complexity of current
   users' activities and interactions in the urban space, and the potential
   future pathways of urban growth and its impact on the environment,
   people and policies as well. The study assesses the following dimensions
   of sustainability: environmental, social, governance and spatial (urban
   form) in Ongata Rongai. GIS and remote sensing technologies were used to
   understand, monitor, model future urban growth and measure the
   sustainability of urban growth. Cellular Automata (CA) is used to
   simulate future LULC of Ongata Rongai. The study finds the urban area
   unstainable and recommends the promotion of the smart growth concept in
   addition to the establishment of an urban board and sensitization of
   public participation.},
