Title = {APPLICATION OF THE MULTI-CRITERIA ANALYSIS FOR DEFINING THE SOCIAL
   FUNCTIONS OF URBAN FORESTS},
Booktitle = {WATER RESOURCES, FOREST, MARINE AND OCEAN ECOSYSTEMS CONFERENCE
   PROCEEDINGS, SGEM 2016, VOL II},
Series = {International Multidisciplinary Scientific GeoConference-SGEM},
Year = {2016},
Pages = {479-486},
Note = {16th International Multidisciplinary Scientific Geoconference (SGEM
   2016), Albena, BULGARIA, JUN 30-JUL 06, 2016},
Organization = {Bulgarian Acad Sci; Acad Sci Czech Republ; Latvian Acad Sci; Polish Acad
   Sci; Russian Acad Sci; Serbian Acad Sci \& Arts; Slovak Acad Sci; Natl
   Acad Sci Ukraine; Inst Water Problem \& Hydropower NAS KR; Natl Acad Sci
   Armenia; Sci Council Japan; World Acad Sci; European Acad Sci Arts \&
   Lett; Acad Sci Moldova; Montenegrin Acad Sci \& Arts; Croatian Acad Sci
   \& Arts; Georgian Natl Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Turkish Acad Sci; Bulgarian Ind Assoc; Bulgarian Minist Environm \&
   Water},
Abstract = {Urban forests are an attractive place of recreation for the population
   of cities and towns. Contact with nature, clean environment and
   proximity of these areas is what makes them attractive. An evaluation of
   their suitability for performing specific functions requires an analysis
   of a number of factors. The land features, vegetation and the presence
   of water reservoirs and other interesting features determine the
   functions that may be assigned to such forests. The literature available
   on the subject contains many references to the ways in which urban
   forests can be managed.
   This article focuses on the social needs and functions that these
   forests can perform. A decision to select a forest to play a specific
   role is primarily conditional upon people's expectations. An entity
   performing the aforementioned analysis defines a set of criteria or its
   different alternatives, which are then subjected to an analysis by means
   of mathematical support of the decision-making process. The criteria are
   understood to mean features of an area which serve as basis for the
   classification and evaluation of physical and geographical criteria over
   a specific area.
   Only a proper analysis of the characteristics of a forest allows
   assigning to it the right functions. The article discusses the methods
   of such analyses. It shows the usefulness of a multi-criteria analysis,
   which allows to draw a map of suitability of forests for specific
   functions. The research focused on developing optimal criteria for
   solving a research task taking into account the relationship between the
   needs of a local community, the environment and the management aspects.
   The article outlines the proposed methodology and the procedure leading
   to determining the suitability of urban forests for specific social
   functions.},
