   07-09, 2017},
Organization = {Malaysian Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {Teachers are vital agents of change in any educational reform, hence, it
   is necessary that their perceptions about action research be explicated.
   In this study, the Perceptions on Action Research Questionnaire was
   developed and validated in order to describe the teachers' views and
   perceptions about action research. Validation of the PARQ was done using
   principal component analysis with orthogonal varimax rotation.
   Bartlett's test of sphericity, X-2(435) = 4743.04, p < .001, indicated
   that correlations between items were sufficiently large for PCA. Given
   the large sample size, and the convergence of the scree plot of the
   questionnaire and Kaiser's criterion, three components were retained in
   the final analysis namely; action research principles; attitudes toward
   doing action research; and processes involved in conducting action
   research. The Perceptions on Action Research Questionnaire (PARQ) used
   in the study was found to be a reliable and valid instrument to measure
   teachers' views on action research. Of the 505 teachers who volunteered
   to participate in this study, more than 90\% of the hold very positive
   perceptions about the basic principles of action research. The teachers
   perceived that by doing action research, they can focus on studying
   their teaching practices and consequently become more effective
   teachers. Valuable insights were drawn from the teachers' responses,
   which may be used as a basis in developing training programs on Action
   Research.},
