   2005},
Organization = {Mediterranean Sci Assoc Environm Protect},
Abstract = {The measurements of the suspended PM10 particles in 5 air pollution
   monitoring stations in Athens basin during the 4-year period 2001-2004
   are analyzed. The stations are grouped into urban stations (Pireas,
   Aristotelous,), located close to urban emissions and into peripheral
   stations (Zografou, Ag. Paraskevi, Thrakomakedones), located at the
   north to east edge of the urban area. The mean concentrations of all
   observations are first calculated and compared with the respective
   values when winds only from the northern sector prevail (with high wind
   speeds occurring most of the time) and secondly when winds only from the
   southern sector dominate. The major findings of this study are: a) The
   PM10 average concentrations of the urban stations show no clear seasonal
   variation but for the peripheral stations the mean of the warm period
   levels are higher than the corresponding cold period levels. b). The
   variations of PM10 concentrations present combined characteristics of
   both primary (NOx, SO2) and secondary (O-3) pollutants. c). The mean
   rural background PM10 levels of the warm period of the year around
   Athens (37 mu g/m(3)), are about the, 63\% of the warm period mean value
   at the urban stations. Such rural background PM10 levels are considered
   high as they are close to the present EU standards and significantly
   higher than the future ones.},
