Organization = {Univ Perugia; Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {Urban accidents have the highest percentage impact (similar to 75\%)
   over the entirety of accidents: therefore they represent a crucial event
   which potentially may lead to disastrous consequences. The understanding
   of this phenomenon is not easy because of the numerous variables which
   must be taken into account. Traditional statistical approaches may be
   not sufficient to tackle this problem and hence new. methods should be
   carried out. Artificial Intelligence may be helpful for providing more
   powerful techniques. In a precious paper some of the authors used neural
   networks to analyse accidents occurred in a small city (about 100,000
   inhabitants). In this paper the same Al methodology is applied to study
   accidents occurred in the metropolitan area of the city of Milan over a
   period of four years. The high number of data gh es to the analysis a
   good statistical significance. The paper describes the methodology used
   to prepare data: it is rattler important to discharge incomplete or
   wrong data: to fill in accidents records with geometrical and flow
   characteristics of road intersections: to calculate an accidents index
   to weigh dangerousness of the place where accidents occurred.},
