   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc},
Abstract = {In the present study, a 3-D geo-database is used to model the urban
   geometry and analyze the spatial variations of summertime nocturnal
   temperature in urban areas of Hong Kong. High resolution raster data
   representing topographical height and vector data representing buildings
   are used to derive a digital elevation model (DEM) of the urban canopy.
   A software method is developed to calculate sky view factor (SVF) based
   on the DEM. Meteorological data obtained in a mobile traverse
   measurement are compared with the resulted SVF. Regression analysis
   confirms the usefulness of areal average of compared elements in
   correlating temperature variations with SVF, and 100m cell average
   appears to be the appropriate scale. The paper further derives an
   overall pattern of Hong Kong's urban heat island intensity quantified by
   SVF for planning concerns.},
