   TRANSPORT; FRENCH DEPT RES \& ENVIRONM},
Abstract = {The following is a support model for urban area planning which allows
   the evaluation of the impact of measures taken regarding motor vehicle
   traffic on air quality. The model allows assignment of traffic flows to
   the road network, calculation of the composite emission factors using
   the EEC-approved J-CORINAIR method, determination of both the emission
   and dispersion of the primary pollutants and production of graphical
   representations of the results. The results of its application in Milan
   to determine the concentration of carbon monoxide and oxides of nitrogen
   caused by urban motor vehicle traffic, have been listed and will serve
   as an example of its effectiveness.},
