Note = {3rd World Conference on Psychology, Counselling and Guidance (WCPCG),
   Efes, TURKEY, MAY 09-12, 2012},
Abstract = {In the national education system of Romania exists a network of offices
   that support school work school counsellors. According to legislation, a
   counsellor serves a total of 800 students. Economic situation really
   makes a counsellor to work with over 1000 students, plus parents and
   teachers. The aim is to identify the role of school counsellor in
   Romania and to identify the perception of students on the importance of
   activities undertaken by school counsellor, using an questionnaire-based
   survey. The research revealed that the main obstacles in the school
   counsellor's activity are related to management of schools, limited
   material resources and large number of beneficiaries. The results show
   that the relationship with the counsellor, students primarily want trust
   and discretion. School counsellor is often exceeded by the large number
   of beneficiaries and the multitude of problems faced. Students perceive
   positively his activity, but is still insufficient awareness of its role
   in school and what services are offered (for free) by the school
   counsellor. (C) 2013 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection
   and peer-review under responsibility of Prof. Dr. Huseyin Uzunboylu \&
