Abstract = {The objective of this study was to examine the effects of a 4-month
   exercise intervention program on physical self-perception (PSP) and
   social physical anxiety (SPA) of non-physically activity adolescent
   China university girls An experimental design with randomization into an
   intervention groups were used The Group A offered to the intervention
   group twice a week for 4-month, which activity was badminton The Group B
   offered to the intervention group twice a week for 4-mionth, consisted
   of badminton sessions followed by 15min of discussions regarding a
   healthy lifestyle Twenty participants in the Group A and twenty in Group
   B completed the Physical Self-Perception Profile (PSPP) and the Social
   Physique Anxiety Scale (SPAS) at pre-test and post-test, in addition,
   physical fitness, weight and height were measured The intent to treat
   analysis showed significant improvements in SPA and PSPP sub domains,
   but Sport Competence (SC) and Physical Strength (PS) were no significant
   improvement By contract Group A and B, Bodily Attractiveness (BA) and
   Physical Self-Worth (PSW) were significant improvement in Group B So
   certain intensity, times, exercise following discussion have meaning
   towards improve Physical self-perception and social physique anxiety in
   university girls},
