Abstract = {At present, research about Urban Heat Island Effects (UHI) is a hot
   issue in urban climate and ecological environment. Because remote
   sensing technology has many advantages, it becomes an important means of
   UHI research. How to use multi-temporal thermal infrared remote sensing
   data and dynamically monitor and evaluate UHI is a N.-cry interesting
   research topic. This article took Luzhou City in Sichuan Province, China
   as an example and explored methods to monitoring and evaluating UHI
   based on Landsat-5 TM data, which obtained on September 15, 1988, and
   Landsat-7 ETM+ data which obtained on August 29, 2002.Technical methods
   and research route established by this article can provide references
