Note = {1st International Conference on Science and Technology Applications in
   Climate Change (STACLIM), INDONESIA, NOV 17-18, 2014},
Abstract = {Land use changes is amodification process due to human activities on the
   environment of natural functions. The analysis of land use changes is
   carried out by using the R Mapper and Map Info Professional 8.5 and land
   use of 1980, 1990, 2000, and 2010. The result showed that land
   development over time increased significantly from 1980 to 1990. This
   impacted the rate of population growth and thus increases anthropogenic
   activities, number of vehicles, and public facilities. This is
   coinciding with the increase of urban heat island (UHI) phenomenon in
   the Kemayoran and Pondok Betung stations in the City of Jakarta.},
