   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {A new urban district has been developed in Xiangtan, a city in Hunan
   province of south China. Low grade energy in surface water and solar
   energy are utilized for the purpose of energy saving and environmental
   improvement, and an open-loop Surface water heat pump (SWHP) system and
   some solar domestic hot water (SDHW) systems were constructed in the
   urban district. This study evaluates the energy and exergy utilization
   efficiencies of renewable energy resources (RERs) by using energy and
   exergy analyses. We found the energy and exergy efficiencies of the SWHP
   system in heating mode to be 395\% and 17.78\%, respectively. The energy
   and exergy efficiencies for the SDHW systems were found to be 34.96\%
   and 17.5\%, respectively. The research results indicate the necessity of
   exergy efficiency improvement. Some measures improving the exergy
   utilization efficiency of RERs are discussed.},
