   Water \& Environm Sci; Minist Educ \& Ciencia; Inst Agua \& Ciencias
   Ambientales; Patronato Municipal Turismo Alicante; Univ Alicante, Grupo
   Invest Modelizac Matemat Sistemas},
Abstract = {Urban runoff pollution due to suspended particles is of great concern
   for sewer system managers. This paper presents a new conceptual model
   called RQSM (Runoff Quality System Model) used to simulate the washoff
   (erosion and transport of particle) of total suspended particles (TSS)
   at the outlet of urban catchments. The RQSM model was validated with the
   help of 285 TSS data points monitored during 22 rainfall events. Four
   rainfall events were monitored in the subcatchment (1) of Verdun borough
   in Canada and 18 rainfall events were monitored on three subcatchments
   in Champaign city (USA). The simulated loads of the RQSM model were
   compared to the simulated loads obtained with the ``rating curve{''}
   model and with the SWMM exponential washoff model. The performance
   criteria showed that the results given by the RQSM model are equivalent
   to the results given by the rating curve model and the SWMM exponential
   washoff model. A sensitivity analysis that was conducted on the RQSM
   model places of interest the influence of every parameter on the
   simulated loads.},
