   SBSI; CIB},
Abstract = {The aim of the research is to develop a sensory evaluation methodology
   for materials, to be shared and spread, taking into account the existing
   research and simplifying it, to make results easily understandable. The
   research has been started from the need to provide students and
   designers with a material library and a virtual database, called MATto
   (Material library of the Industrial Design Course at the Politecnico di
   Torino), about innovative materials useful for the industrial product
   and project.
   Well known technical tools will be used, such as the Sensotact by
   Renault, to carry out a tactile evaluation of materials, but also
   innovative tools will be utilized within the research, such as
   eye-tracking. Another fundamental tool to use in sensory evaluations is,
   of course, the human being: a group of ``material tasters{''}.
   One specific aim is the creation of a simplified ``sensory
   vocabulary{''}, a tool for the designer that defines, through value
   scales, footages and sounds, the ``describing adjectives{''}, previously
   detected by the tasters' panel.
   Analysed materials, from a technical, environmental and
   expressive-sensory point of view, are deeply involved in the development
   of project concepts for different sectors and they are also a tool to
   create, develop, analyse and finally test, using tools such as
   eye-tracking, project and metaproject concepts.},
