   19-21, 2018},
Abstract = {The main purpose of this study is to investigate NO2 temporal
   distribution in two urban areas in Romania based on data measured by
   stationary monitoring stations during 2016 and 2017. Analysis of the
   measurement data show that NO2 emissions from traffic type sources has a
   higher contribution to the urban pollution than industry type source.
   The analysis of emission trend in the two cities (for 2 years), shows an
   effective reduction in emissions from industrial type source but an
   increase in emissions from traffic type source with 12.88 to 28.45 \%.
