Note = {Conference on Improving Sustainability Concept in Developing Countries
   (ISCDC), Cairo, EGYPT, DEC 02-04, 2015},
Abstract = {The research probed the residents' awareness of climate change,
   perception of risk and their preparedness for natural disasters in the
   urban poor community of BASECO in Manila, Philippines. Using a
   structural equation model (SEM) for predicting building resilience and
   increasing adaptive capacity validates the hypothesis for risk
   perception in the context of the urban poor and the structural
   constraints that subjugates the high level of risk perception. The study
   highlights the importance of understanding the risk perceptions and
   responses to climate change and natural disasters with social, economic,
   political and cultural perspectives to ensure participation in building
   resilience and increasing adaptive capacity. (C) 2016 The Authors.
   Published by Elsevier B.V.},
