   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {This work presents the results of studies in urban areas or urban
   expansion areas in Descalvado, SP relating to the development of the
   erosive process in function of the action of the physical environment,
   such as: geological formation, declivity, climate, soil use and
   geotechnical attributes of the unconsolidated materials (physical index,
   M.C.T. classification and erodibility index).
   The data analysis made possible to classify homogenous areas in terms of
   potentiality of the erosive process in terms of weathering profiles in
   diabases and sedimentaries rocks. As a final product was manufactured a
   geotechnical map, in 1:10,000 scale, have accelerated potential.},
